``` Brute force: more than 10 failed logons (4625) per account within any 5-minute sliding window.
``` Data: index=win_dc, sourcetype=XmlWinEventLog (Universal Forwarder with renderXml=true).
``` Validated in the lab on 2026-10-29 against the 2026-10-03 bursts (Eval 01, 02, 02b).
``` Notes:
```  - lower(user): Windows account names are case-insensitive (Administrator = administrator).
```  - src_ip instead of IpAddress: IpAddress is extracted twice in this lab (duplicate multivalue).
```  - streamstats time_window=5m needs events in time order (sort 0 _time).
```  - Burst grouping: a new burst starts after a gap of more than 5 minutes; one row per incident.
```  - The lookup adds asset context. 10.0.20.120 (GREENBONE01) is an authorized scanner: tune by
```    scan window, not by a permanent IP exclusion.

index=win_dc sourcetype=XmlWinEventLog EventCode=4625 user=* user!="-"
| eval account=lower(user)
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=5m count as fails_5m by account
| streamstats current=f last(_time) as prev_time by account
| eval new_burst=if(isnull(prev_time) OR _time-prev_time>300, 1, 0)
| streamstats sum(new_burst) as burst_id by account
| stats count as total_failures max(fails_5m) as peak_fails_5m values(SubStatus) as substatus min(_time) as first_time max(_time) as last_time by account burst_id src_ip
| where peak_fails_5m > 10
| stats dc(account) as accounts_hit sum(total_failures) as failures values(substatus) as substatus min(first_time) as first_time max(last_time) as last_time by src_ip
| lookup lab_assets.csv ip as src_ip OUTPUT hostname role zone authorized_activity
| convert ctime(first_time) ctime(last_time)
| sort - failures
